{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgANkCWpdkT9vgepAcHRc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `Hijack` in `response_writer.go` so it fails only after body bytes have been written (`size > 0`). Before, it also failed when only the headers had been sent (`size == 0`). That broke websocket libraries that call `WriteHeaderNow` or `Flush` before hijacking. Hijacking still fails once any body data has been written.\n\nI added a \"hijack after header flush should succeed\" case to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite`. The gate passed: the new test fails without the fix and passes with it, and the format and leftover-debug checks were clean.\n\nI only ran the `TestResponseWriterHijack*` tests, not the full suite or a real websocket library."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1184,"cache_read_input_tokens":33559,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1184,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":228,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99fa3d9c-69db-4045-8fa3-94975e0b7656","uuid":"e0d110ab-10be-4fff-b14c-3cff8aea14a2","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:00:27.169Z","request_id":"req_011CgANkCGh3eV57vfGwYDgv"}
